            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CLR1966"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn't add the foil. They came out perfect and fluffier than any we've made in the regular oven! Will never cook them any other way again. Thanks for the super-easy idea!",
            "datePublished": "2026-02-23T17:33:26.283Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "macc"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great but I found 4 hours on high too long, but I did mine with one potato in foil and a pork loin chop in foil and a mug of baked beans. This was a lovely dinner for one.",
            "datePublished": "2025-11-12T15:06:46.073Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kate"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These baked potatoes always come out of my crock pot steamy hot, well cooked and ready to serve with sour cream, chives and bacon toppings. So easy! I start them around noon and cook them on high for 5-6 hours. Really makes meal prep so simple, and who doesn't love a loaded baked potato! (Note: We live at an altitude of 7,400 feet above sea level, so our cooking times are usually longer than most recipes call for.)",
            "datePublished": "2025-04-15T00:43:37.346Z"
          },
